docs {
  # Enduser authorized parties scenarios

  BDD scenarios for `GET /accessmanagement/api/v1/enduser/authorizedparties`.

  Each subfolder is one scenario. The files inside are the scenario steps, named
  `NN_GIVEN|WHEN|THEN|AND|CLEANUP_...` and ordered by `seq`. Scenarios are independent of
  each other and can run standalone, and anything a scenario creates it removes again, so
  the whole folder can run repeatedly against a shared environment.

  ## Response shape

  The endpoint returns a paginated envelope, `{ "links": { "next": ... }, "data": [ ... ] }`.
  Every step reads the party list from `res.getBody().data`.

  A party carries `partyUuid`, `name`, `organizationNumber`, `parentId`, `personId`,
  `dateOfBirth`, `partyId`, `emailId`, `type`, `unitType`, `isDeleted`,
  `onlyHierarchyElementWithNoAccess`, `authorizedAccessPackages`, `authorizedResources`,
  `authorizedRoles`, `authorizedInstances` and `subunits`. Subunits are nested under their
  main unit rather than listed at the top level.

  ## Authorization

  The endpoint is behind the `EnduserAuthorizedParty` policy, which accepts either the
  `altinn:portal/enduser` scope or `altinn:accessmanagement/authorizedparties`. The caller
  is resolved from the user id claim, falling back to the system user uuid.

  ## Personas and fixtures

  - `test/AuthorizedParties/testdata/<env>.js`: the accounting firm tree around
    REGN_ULASTELIG_RETTFERDIG_TIGER, its clients, rightholders, deleted sole
    proprietorships, self identified users and the system user.
  - `testdata/auth-parties-testdata/<env>.js`: the main unit / subunit / person matrix used
    by the delegation direction scenario.

  ## Environments

  Runs against AT22.
}
